  <static seed="123" source="Library/Michigan/Chap3Sec4/Q71.pg">
    <statement><p>Given
<m>F(2)=1, F'(2)=1, F(3)=1, F'(3)=3</m> and
<m>G(1)=4, G'(1)=2, G(3)=2, G'(3)=3</m>,
find each of the following.
(Enter <alert>dne</alert> for any derivative that cannot be
computed from this information alone.)</p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p><m>H(3)</m>  if <m>H(x)=F(G(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H'(3)</m> if <m>H(x)=F(G(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H(3)</m>  if <m>H(x)=G(F(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H'(3)</m> if <m>H(x)=G(F(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H'(3)</m> if <m>H(x)=F(x)/G(x)</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1\cdot 3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot 3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3\cdot 2-1\cdot 3}{2^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>H(x) = F(G(x))</m>,



<m>H(3) = F(G(3)) = F(2) = 1</m>



<m>H'(3) = F'(G(3))\cdot G'(3) = F'(2)\cdot 3 = 
   1\cdot 3 = 3</m>



For <m>H(x) = G(F(x))</m>, 



<m>H(3) = G(F(3)) = G(1) = 4</m>



<m>H'(3) = G'(F(3))\cdot F'(3) = G'(1)\cdot 3 = 
   2\cdot 3 = 6</m>



For <m>H(x) = F(x)/G(x)</m>, 



<m>H'(3) = \frac{F'(3) G(3) - F(3) G'(3)}{G(3)^2}
   = \frac{ (3)(2) - (1)(3) } {2^2} = 0.75</m>.



</solution>
